==Russian==
{{wikipedia|lang=ru}}
===Etymology===
Apparently from {{etyl|en|ru}} {{term|Vauxhall}} (site of a pleasure garden and major railway station); or from German [[Volk]] + [[Saal]] or from Dutch [[volk]] + [[zaal]] (people’s hall).

===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|Ru-вокзал.ogg|audio}}
*{{IPA|/vɐˈgzal/}}

===Noun===
'''вокзал''' (vokzál) {{m}}

# {{obsolete|lang=ru}} [[park]], [[pleasure garden]]
#*'''1813''', Aleksandr Pushkin, ‘To Natalie’
#*:''На гуляньях иль в '''воксалах''' / Легким зефиром летал.''  At fetes and in parks, I've been flitting like a gentle zephyr.
# [[train station]], [[railroad station]], [[railway station]], [[depot]]

